    "result_text": "All 30 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-day owner-creation cap in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler):\n\n```java\nLocalDate today = LocalDate.now();\nlong createdToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))\n    .count();\nif (createdToday >= 100) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n}\n```\n\nPlaced early in `addOwner`, it counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and returns **429 Too Many Requests** once that count reaches 100, rejecting the 101st create of the day. `LocalDate` and `HttpStatus` were already imported.\n\nThe existing acceptance test `Cp19Tests` (which creates 100 owners dated today, then expects the 101st to be rejected with 429) now passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 **30 tests run, 0 failures**.",
